# Rank 1022 / CVE-2024-35255: the Azure Identity Arc managed-identity source
# took the key-file path straight out of the WWW-Authenticate challenge returned
# by the local IMDS endpoint and read it, then sent the contents as a Basic
# authorization header. Whoever can answer that endpoint therefore chooses which
# file is read and receives its contents, which is an elevation of privilege.
# The fixed revision adds ValidatePath: the name must end in .key, the path must
# sit under the platform's token directory, and the file must be at most 4096
# bytes.
#
# ATTENTION, two engine gaps, both isolated with minimal pairs.
#
# First, taint does not cross a C# out parameter. In the real file both ends are
# labelled, response.Headers.TryGetValue as code.HttpInput and
# File.ReadAllText as code.FilePathAccess, yet trace reports the source has no
# outgoing flow at all. The pair below shows why: the identical read written
# through an out parameter produces nothing, while the same read taking the
# value from a return value is reported as VYQL-PATH-001. This is not specific
# to this CVE. TryGetValue, TryParse and the whole Try-prefixed family deliver
# their value through out, so any tainted string arriving that way is invisible
# in C#.
#
# Second, a containment check is not recognised as a path control in C#. Even
# with the value arriving by return, adding the fixed revision's own guard, EndsWith(".key")
# plus StartsWith against the expected token directory, leaves the finding in
# place, whether the guard sits in a helper or is inlined. Only Path.GetFullPath,
# Path.GetFileName and safePath emit core.PathCanonicalization for C#, and
# StartsWith appears solely inside case-specific negations rather than as a
# reusable control. Python suppresses the equivalent realpath plus
# startswith shape, so the two frontends disagree. Recognising it precisely
# needs the guard-to-branch relationship, the same missing fact rank 1013 ran
# into.
#
# Closing only the first gap would report the vulnerable code but also the
# patched code, so this rank needs both before it can report.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1022: tainted value delivered through an out parameter reaches the file read unseen"
  lang csharp
  file sdk/identity/Azure.Identity/src/AzureArcManagedIdentitySource.cs
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  using System.IO;

  public class AzureArcManagedIdentitySource
  {
      public string ReadKeyFile(Response response)
      {
          if (!response.Headers.TryGetValue("WWW-Authenticate", out string challenge))
          {
              return null;
          }
          return File.ReadAllText(challenge);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1022: the same read is reported when the value arrives as a return value"
  lang csharp
  file sdk/identity/Azure.Identity/src/AzureArcManagedIdentitySource.cs
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  using System.IO;

  public class AzureArcManagedIdentitySource
  {
      public string ReadKeyFile(Response response)
      {
          string challenge = response.Headers.GetValue("WWW-Authenticate");
          return File.ReadAllText(challenge);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1022: the fixed revision's directory containment guard does not suppress the finding"
  lang csharp
  file sdk/identity/Azure.Identity/src/AzureArcManagedIdentitySource.cs
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  using System;
  using System.IO;

  public class AzureArcManagedIdentitySource
  {
      public string ReadKeyFile(Response response)
      {
          string challenge = response.Headers.GetValue("WWW-Authenticate");
          var expectedPath = Path.Combine("/", "var", "opt", "azcmagent", "tokens");
          if (!challenge.EndsWith(".key") || !challenge.StartsWith(expectedPath))
          {
              throw new AuthenticationFailedException("The secret key file failed validation.");
          }
          return File.ReadAllText(challenge);
      }
  }
  ```
